We'll need to be careful about ordering: we need to have transport leg assembled and loading authorized before we can mark origin/destination dispatch ready and before loading container onto leg for beta.

Thus we need to prepare origin and destination availabilities (including load/unload) first, then assemble transport leg, authorize loading, then mark origin/destination dispatch ready, then allocate/dispatch them, then handle shift alpha (operator, constraint, compliance, finalize, allocate/dispatch), then shift beta (vehicle allocate, operator, skill cert, load container, stage, verify loading, assign compliance, establish clearance, finalize, allocate/dispatch). However note that shift beta needs transport leg assembled and loading authorized before loading container (load_container_onto_leg requires transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized). So we need to assemble and authorize before loading container for beta. That's fine.

But shift beta also needs candidate_prepared, candidate_task_profile_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_skill_certificate_linked before loading container? load_container_onto_leg does not require operator or skill certificate. It only requires candidate_prepared, candidate_transport_leg_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_available, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we can load container before linking operator and skill certificate. However verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_operator_linked and candidate_skill_certificate_linked. So we need to link operator and skill certificate before verification.

Thus order for beta: after preparing (vehicle allocate, task profile link, confirm preparedness), we can load container onto leg (after transport leg ready), then stage, then assign operator and skill certificate, then verify loading, then assign compliance, establish clearance, finalize, allocate/dispatch.

